#!/bin/bash
# Teria Bootprotokolle: legt Logs dieses Starts auf der FAT32-Partition der SD ab (teria-logs/),
# damit sie sich am PC/Mac lesen lassen. Die letzten 5 Starts bleiben erhalten.
set -u
# shellcheck source=os/teria-base/usr/lib/teria/lib.sh
. "${TERIA_LIB:-/usr/lib/teria}/lib.sh"
SD=$(sd_mount) || exit 0
D="$SD/teria-logs/$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
mkdir -p "$D"
{
    echo "== $(date) | $(uname -a)"; cat /proc/cmdline; echo
    cat /etc/os-release; echo
    systemctl --failed --no-pager; echo
    systemctl status lightdm display-manager nv-l4t-usb-device-mode NetworkManager teria-firstboot teria-setup --no-pager -l 2>&1; echo
    loginctl list-seats --no-pager; loginctl seat-status seat0 --no-pager 2>&1 | head -60; echo
    ip -br addr; nmcli -t general 2>&1; nmcli -t dev 2>&1; echo
    ls -la /dev/fb* /dev/dri /dev/nvhost-ctrl /dev/tegra_dc_* 2>&1; echo
    chage -l teria 2>&1
} > "$D/uebersicht.txt" 2>&1
journalctl -b 0 --no-pager -o short-monotonic > "$D/journal.txt" 2>&1
journalctl -b 0 -p warning --no-pager > "$D/journal-warnungen.txt" 2>&1
cp /var/log/Xorg.0.log "$D/" 2>/dev/null
cp /var/log/lightdm/*.log "$D/" 2>/dev/null
dmesg > "$D/dmesg.txt" 2>&1
# nur die letzten 5 Starts behalten
find "$SD/teria-logs" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d -print0 | sort -z | head -z -n -5 | xargs -0 -r rm -rf
sync
umount "$SD" 2>/dev/null
exit 0
